generic layer-4 TCP tarpit for abusive clients.

tcptarpit accepts connections that pf(4) diverts to it via rdr-to -
for example sources overloaded into a <bruteforcers> table by
max-src-conn-rate rules - and never sends a single byte back.  Incoming
data is read and discarded, so the trapped client waits for a response
that never comes while its TCP window runs full.  Connections are held
until the client gives up or a configurable hold time expires.

The package creates the unprivileged daemon user _tcptarpit and
installs the rc.d(8) script; the daemon runs as _tcptarpit without any
manual steps.

Configuration lives in /etc/tcptarpit.conf (sample in
/usr/local/share/examples/tcptarpit/); enable and start the daemon
with:

	rcctl enable tcptarpit
	rcctl start tcptarpit
